# SABOTAGE: issue #25 step 3 — the registration-time `validations` block is REMOVED from
# `Samen.Scopes.Primitives.Blueprint.define_webhook/5`, so nothing stops a tenant from
# SAVING a `webhook` endpoint row whose `url` is `http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/`,
# `https://127.0.0.1/hook`, `http://[::1]/hook`, an IPv4-mapped private address, or a
# `file:` scheme. The row persists; the defect then lives in the tenant's own
# configuration, waiting for the delivery path to be the only thing between it and the
# metadata service.
#
# Flips the named reds in `test/egress/url_validation_test.exs`, which builds a real
# `Ash.Changeset.for_create/3` against the Primitives-scope `webhook` resource mounted in
# samen_core's own test tree (`SamenCore.Support.NotificationFixture.Webhook`, abbrev
# `nwh`) — the SAME `define_webhook/5` blueprint every host mounts — and asserts a
# FIELD-SCOPED error on `:url`. With the block gone there is no `:url` error to find.
#
# The POSITIVE CONTROL in the same file still PASSES — a public `https` URL produces no
# `:url` error on create OR update — which is what makes the red mean what it says: the
# assertion is field-scoped, so an unrelated required-attribute error can neither
# manufacture a pass on the red nor break the control.
#
# NOT TOUCHED, deliberately: `Samen.Egress.UrlValidation` and `Samen.Egress.Guard`
# themselves (still compiled, still correct, just not WIRED — the "the guard exists, it is
# simply never asked" shape), the delivery-time authority in `Samen.Webhook.DeliveryWorker`
# (351 owns that), `:autoredirect` (350 owns that), the resource's attributes, its `pii`
# block, its `reveal_webhook` action and its policies. The moduledoc STILL documents the
# write-time refusal, so the resource advertises a guard it no longer runs.
#
# Deletes one contiguous `validations` block and replaces it with a `# SABOTAGE` comment,
# so the macro still expands and the file compiles under `--warnings-as-errors`. Touches
# blueprint.ex ALONE.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/egress/url_validation_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: #25 RED: a cloud-metadata URL cannot be registered
# MUST_FAIL: #25 RED: a loopback URL cannot be registered
# MUST_FAIL: #25 RED: an RFC1918 URL cannot be registered
# MUST_FAIL: #25 RED: a non-http(s) scheme cannot be registered
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/primitives/blueprint.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/primitives/blueprint.ex
